isBrowserLoading.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0150|1.5||

This function checks if a browser is currently loading a website.

}}

loadBrowserURL.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0150|1.5||

This function loads the specified URL.

* **Note:** You should use [requestBrowserDomains](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/requestBrowserDomains) first to request permission to load the url on the client.

* **Note:** Calling loadBrowserURL right after [createBrowser](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/createBrowser) will not work normally due to the nature of the asynchronous browser interface. Refer to [onClientBrowserCreated](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientBrowserCreated) for more information.

}}

navigateBrowserBack.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0153|1.5.3|9912|

Returns the browser to the previous page.

}}

navigateBrowserForward.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0153|1.5.3|9912|

This function takes the browser to the next page.

}}

reloadBrowserPage.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0153|1.5.3|9912|

This function reloads the current browser's page.

}}

requestBrowserDomains.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0150|1.5||

This function opens a request window in order to accept the requested remote URLs.

* **Note:** You must use this function prior to calling [loadBrowserURL](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/loadBrowserURL) because every domain, with exceptions in the whitelist [https://github.com/multitheftauto/mtasa-blue/blob/505467ec8c3ac1b3ad17fb0247dc15809e013968/Client/cefweb/CWebCore.cpp#L280-L283 here] and [https://github.com/multitheftauto/mtasa-blue/blob/505467ec8c3ac1b3ad17fb0247dc15809e013968/Client/cefweb/CWebCore.cpp#L205-L206 there], is blocked by default.

}}

resizeBrowser.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0153|1.5.3|9912|

Allows resizing of CEF browsers at runtime.

}}

{{Warning|Do *not* use this function with [onClientRender](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientRender) as it re-creates the underlying texture internally (which is an expensive operation).|true}}

setBrowserAjaxHandler.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0151|1.5.1||

This function provides a requestable ajax resource for Lua/Javascript communication for a [Element/Browser|browser](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Browser|browser).

}}

setBrowserProperty.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0150|1.5||

This function sets a given property of a specified browser.

}}

setBrowserRenderingPaused.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0150|1.5||

This function sets the rendering state of a browser.

}}

{{MessageBox|bordercolorhex=FFB2B2|bgcolorhex=FFE5E5|image=File:Dialog-warning.png|title=Warning:|message=May cause issues with browser rendering on PC with low Ram [https://github.com/multitheftauto/mtasa-blue/issues/1567 #1567]. It's might be better to completely release browser, instead of pausing it, when its not needed.}}

setBrowserVolume.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0150|1.5||

This function sets either a specific [Element/Browser|browser](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Browser|browser)'s volume, or the overall volume for browsers.

}}

toggleBrowserDevTools.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0150|1.5||

This function toggles the visibility of the developer tools pane.

}}

* **Note:** You should do a 'setDevelopmentMode(true, true)' before using this function.

createBuilding.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0161|1.6.0|22410|Creates a [building](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/building) [element](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/element) at a given position &amp; interior with a certain rotation.}}

* **Note:** Some [Object|objects](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Object|objects)/[Building|buildings](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Building|buildings) in *interior 13* show in all interiors.

* **Note:** Unlike [createObject](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/createObject), this function does not have an *isLowLOD* argument. When using [setLowLODElement](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/setLowLODElement), the system will automatically define the building as a LOD.

{{BuildingInfo}}

getCamera.description:
{{New items|3.0135|1.3.5|

This function returns an [element](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/element) that corresponds to the game camera

}}

* **Note:** Using attachElements with the camera and the main player can interfere with movement

* **Note:** Using setElementPosition/Rotation/Matrix on the camera element will automatically clear any target set with [setCameraTarget](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/setCameraTarget)

setCameraFieldOfView.description:
{{client function}}

{{New feature/item|3.0151|1.5.1|7397|This function sets the field of view of the ''dynamic camera'' - this is the field of view of the ''non-fixed camera'' - yes, the camera that the user can control whilst on foot or in a vehicle. The higher the field of view angle, the more you will be able to see to your sides.}}

* **Note:** [setCameraFieldOfView](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/setCameraFieldOfView) overrides the user game option in *''Settings-&gt;Video-&gt;FOV*''

* **Note:** [setCameraFieldOfView](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/setCameraFieldOfView) does not affect the FOV for the following camera modes: 1) Player aiming 2) Vehicle front bumper camera 3) Fixed camera

shakeCamera.description:
{{Added feature/item|1.6.1|1.6.0|22631|

This function allows you to trigger camera shake effect (just like explosion does).

}}

* **Note:** The camera shaking duration depends on the force. High values ​​can result in very long durations

resetShakeCamera.description:
{{Added feature/item|1.6.1|1.6.0|22631|

This function cancels the chaking effect caused by *shakeCamera*

}}

dxCreateRenderTarget.description:
This function creates a render target element, which is a special type of [texture](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/texture) that can be drawn on with the dx functions. Successful render target creation is not guaranteed, and may fail due to hardware or memory limitations.

To see if creation is likely to fail, use [dxGetStatus](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/dxGetStatus). (When *VideoMemoryFreeForMTA* is zero, failure ''is'' guaranteed.)

{{Tip|Use [dxSetBlendMode](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/dxSetBlendMode) to get better quality}}

{{Tip|It is highly recommended that [dxSetTestMode](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/dxSetTestMode) is used when writing and testing scripts using dxCreateRenderTarget.}}

* **Note:** Render targets are usually cleared when the player minimizes MTA (i.e. alt-tab). See [onClientRestore](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientRestore) for details on when to restore any fixed content.

dxDrawCircle.description:
{{Client Function}}

&lt;lowercasetitle/&gt;

{{New feature/item|3.0156|1.5.5|13977|This function draws a circle shape on the screen - rendered for *one* frame.  This should be used in conjunction with [onClientRender](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientRender) in order to be display continuously.}}

dxDrawImage.description:
[Image:MTAsa dxDrawImage.png|thumb|190px|An image drawn on the screen with the dxDrawImage function.](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Image:MTAsa dxDrawImage.png|thumb|190px|An image drawn on the screen with the dxDrawImage function.)

Draws an image on the screen for a single frame. In order for the image to stay visible continuously, you need to call this function with the same parameters on each frame update (see [onClientRender](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientRender)).&lt;br/&gt;

Image files should ideally have dimensions that are a power of two, to prevent possible blurring.&lt;br/&gt;

&lt;b&gt;Power of two: 2px, 4px, 8px, 16px, 32px, 64px, 128px, 256px, 512px, 1024px...&lt;/b&gt;

{{Important Note|Do not draw image from path. Use a texture created with [dxCreateTexture](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/dxCreateTexture) instead to *efficiently draw image*.}}

{{Important Note|For further optimising your DX code, see [dxCreateRenderTarget](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/dxCreateRenderTarget). You should use render target whenever possible, in order to dramatically reduce CPU usage caused by many dxDraw* calls.}}

{{Tip|To help prevent edge artifacts when drawing textures, set *textureEdge* to *"clamp"* when calling [dxCreateTexture](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/dxCreateTexture).}}

dxDrawImageSection.description:
Differing from [dxDrawImage](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/dxDrawImage), this function only draws a part of an image on the screen for a single frame. In order for the image to stay visible continuously, you need to call this function with the same parameters on each frame update (see [onClientRender](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientRender)).

Image files should ideally have dimensions that are a power of two, to prevent possible blurring.&lt;br/&gt;

&lt;b&gt;Power of two: 2px, 4px, 8px, 16px, 32px, 64px, 128px, 256px, 512px, 1024px...&lt;/b&gt;

{{Tip|Use a texture created with [dxCreateTexture](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/dxCreateTexture) to *speed up drawing*.}}

{{Tip|To help prevent edge artifacts when drawing textures, set *textureEdge* to *"clamp"* when calling [dxCreateTexture](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/dxCreateTexture)}}

dxDrawLine3D.description:
This function draws a 3D line between two points in the 3D world - rendered for *one* frame.  This should be used in conjunction with [onClientRender](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientRender) in order to display continuously.

{{Legacy|legacy/DxDrawLine3D}}

{{Updated feature/item|1.5.9|1.5.9|22465|

dxDrawMaterialPrimitive.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0157|1.5.6|14370|This function draws a 2D primitive shape with material applied to it across the screen - rendered for one frame. This should be used in conjunction with [onClientRender](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientRender) in order to display continuously.

If image file is used, it should ideally have dimensions that are a power of two, to prevent possible blurring.

Power of two: 2px, 4px, 8px, 16px, 32px, 64px, 128px, 256px, 512px, 1024px...}}

dxDrawModel3D.description:
{{Important Note|You can not use this function to draw vehicles and ped}}

{{Important Note|This function doesn't obey any streaming limits, you can draw as many models as you want}}

{{Important Note|You can not render model to render target.}}

{{New feature/item|3.0161|1.6.0|22708|

This function draws a 3D model - rendered for *one* frame. Drawn models are indistinguishable from this one created by [createObject](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/createObject) function. This should be used in conjunction with [onClientRender](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientRender) or [onClientPreRender](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientPreRender) in order to display continuously. Note that a model must be loaded at the time this function is called. A model can be loaded and unloaded with the help of [engineStreamingRequestModel](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/engineStreamingRequestModel) and [engineStreamingReleaseModel](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/engineStreamingReleaseModel) functions.

}}

dxDrawPrimitive3D.description:
This function draws a 3D primitive in the 3D world - rendered for *one* frame.  This should be used in conjunction with [onClientRender](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientRender) in order to display continuously.

{{Legacy|legacy/dxDrawPrimitive3D}}

{{Updated feature/item|1.5.9|1.5.9|22465|

dxGetTexturePixels.description:
This function fetches the [Texture_pixels|pixels](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Texture_pixels|pixels) from a [texture](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/texture) element. It can be used with a standard texture, render target or screen source.

{{Important Note|If the user has not enabled screen uploading in the settings, the function will use a 32x32 empty texture as a basis.}}

{{Note|

*This function is slow and not something you want to be doing once a frame.

*It is slower when reading pixels from a render target or screen source.

*And is very slow indeed if the texture format is not * 'argb' * (unless the native *'dds*' format is used with correct options).

}}

dxIsAspectRatioAdjustmentEnabled.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0140|1.3.3|5547|

This function gets the current aspect ratio set by [dxSetAspectRatioAdjustmentEnabled](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/dxSetAspectRatioAdjustmentEnabled).

}}

dxSetAspectRatioAdjustmentEnabled.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0140|1.3.3|5547|

This function allows for the positioning of dxDraw calls to be automatically adjusted according to the client's aspect ratio setting.  This lasts for a single execution of an event handler for one of the following events: [onClientRender](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientRender), [onClientPreRender](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientPreRender) and [onClientHUDRender](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientHUDRender). So the function has to be called every frame, just like dxDraws.

This is particularly useful for draws that must align with the GTA HUD, for which the sizing and positioning can vary for different aspect ratios.

}}

dxSetShaderTessellation.description:
{{Needs Checking|The example should depict better how does this function actually work with a texture.}}

This function sets the amount of geometric sub-division to use when drawing a [shader](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/shader) element with [dxDrawImage](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/dxDrawImage).

Using tessellation allows a shader to manipulate the shape of the rendered image at each sub-division boundary.

dxSetTextureEdge.description:
{{New items|3.0135|1.3.5|

This functions allows you to change the edge handling after creating the texture.

}}

[File:TextureEdges.jpg|600px](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/File:TextureEdges.jpg|600px)

dxSetTexturePixels.description:
This function sets the [Texture_pixels|pixels](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Texture_pixels|pixels) of a [texture](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/texture) element. It can be used with a standard texture, render target or screen source. Only *'plain*' format pixels please.

{{Note|

* This function is slow and not something you want to be doing once a frame.

* It is very slow when setting pixels to a render target or screen source.

* And is very slow indeed if the texture format is not *"argb"*.

}}

createEffect.description:
{{New items|3.0140|1.4|

Creates an [Element/Effect|effect](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Effect|effect) on specified position.

}}

* **Note:** Not all effects support rotation (e.g. the "fire" - effect doesn't).

* **Note:** All effects have their own duration.

getEffectDensity.description:
{{New items|3.014|1.4 r6208|

This function gets the density of certain [effect](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/effect).

}}

getEffectSpeed.description:
{{New items|3.014|1.4 r6208|

This function gets the speed of a specified [effect](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/effect).

}}

setEffectDensity.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0140|1.4|6208|

This function sets the density of a specified [effect](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/effect).

}}

{{Warning|Upper density limit of this function depends on client FX Quality setting.

The limit is 1 for Low, 1.5 for Medium, and 2 for High/Very high.|true}}

setEffectSpeed.description:
{{New items|3.014|1.4 r6208|

This function sets the speed of a specified [effect](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/effect).

}}

getElementBoneMatrix.description:
{{Added feature/item|1.5.9|1.5.8|20704|This function returns the transformation matrix of a specific bone. Currently the [Element/Player|Player](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Player|Player) and [Element/Ped|Ped](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Ped|Ped) element types are accepted.}}

{{Tip|If you want to attach an element to a bone, see [attachElementToBone](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/attachElementToBone).}}

{{Tip|For [matrix](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/matrix) manipulation which goes beyond the basic examples given on this page, see the [Lua matrix library](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Lua matrix library). Using the built-in [matrix](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/matrix) class is also recommended.}}

getElementBoneQuaternion.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0161|1.6.0|22741|

This function retrieves how a particular bone rotates in relation to the element.&lt;br/&gt;

The use of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quaternion quaternions] are more effective and do not generate issues like gimbal lock that might arise with [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euler_angles Euler angles], so they are a preferable choice for rotation.

}}

isElementCollidableWith.description:
This function can be used to check whether specified element is collidable with another element.&lt;br&gt;

*Note:* You can only use this function with the element types listed below.

*[Player](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Player)

*[Ped](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Ped)

*[Vehicle](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Vehicle)

*[Object](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Object)

{{Added feature/item|1.5.9|1.5.8|21348|

* [Element/Weapon|Weapon](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Weapon|Weapon)

}}

isElementStreamedIn.description:
This function checks whether an [element](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/element) is currently streamed in (not virtualized) and are actual GTA objects in the world. You can force an element to be streamed in using [setElementStreamable](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/setElementStreamable).&lt;br&gt;

{{Deprecated feature|3|1.0|

DP2 can return true even if this element is not fully streamed in. This can happen during the period when the vehicle/object model is loading while the element is not actually fully created yet.

}}

setElementBoneMatrix.description:
{{Added feature/item|1.5.9|1.5.8|20704|This function sets the transformation matrix of a specific bone. Currently the [Element/Player|Player](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Player|Player) and [Element/Ped|Ped](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Ped|Ped) element types are accepted.}}

{{Tip|If you want to attach an element to a bone, see [attachElementToBone](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/attachElementToBone).}}

{{Tip|For [matrix](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/matrix) manipulation which goes beyond the basic examples given on this page, see the [Lua matrix library](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Lua matrix library). Using the built-in [matrix](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/matrix) class is also recommended.}}

setElementBonePosition.description:
{{Added feature/item|1.5.9|1.5.8|20704|This function sets the position of a bone to the specified coordinates. Currently the [Element/Player|Player](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Player|Player) and [Element/Ped|Ped](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Ped|Ped) element types are accepted.}}

{{Tip|If you want to attach an element to a bone, see [attachElementToBone](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/attachElementToBone).}}

* **Note:** You need to use this function together with [onClientPedsProcessed](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientPedsProcessed).

setElementBoneRotation.description:
{{Added feature/item|1.5.9|1.5.8|20704|This function sets the rotation of a specific bone relative to the element. Currently the [Element/Player|Player](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Player|Player) and [Element/Ped|Ped](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Ped|Ped) element types are accepted.}}

{{Tip|If you want to attach an element to a bone, see [attachElementToBone](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/attachElementToBone).}}

* **Note:** [updateElementRpHAnim](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/updateElementRpHAnim) must be called after this function to apply bone rotation.

setElementBoneQuaternion.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0161|1.6.0|22741|

This function determines how a particular bone rotates in relation to the element.&lt;br/&gt;

The use of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quaternion quaternions] are more effective and do not generate issues like gimbal lock that might arise with [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euler_angles Euler angles], so they are a preferable choice for rotation.

}}

{{Tip|If you want to attach an element to a bone, see [attachElementToBone](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/attachElementToBone).}}

* **Note:** If you want to apply the rotation, [updateElementRpHAnim](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/updateElementRpHAnim) must be called after this function.

setElementCollidableWith.description:
This function can be used to set an element to collide with another element. An element with collisions disabled does not interact physically with the other element.&lt;br&gt;

*Note:* You can only use this function with the element types listed below.

*[Player](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Player)

*[Ped](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Ped)

*[Vehicle](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Vehicle)

*[Object](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Object)

{{Added feature/item|1.5.9|1.5.8|21348|

* [Element/Weapon|Weapon](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Weapon|Weapon)

}}

engineLoadIMG.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0161|1.6.0|21708|This function loads an IMG container into GTA.

}}

{{Note|

If you're experiencing crashes/game hangs with default values, try to adjust memory/buffer/cache sizes with [engineStreamingSetMemorySize](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/engineStreamingSetMemorySize), [engineStreamingSetBufferSize](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/engineStreamingSetBufferSize) and/or [engineStreamingSetModelCacheLimits](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/engineStreamingSetModelCacheLimits).}}

engineLoadIFP.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0156|1.5.5|12195|

This function loads an animation library (IFP) file into GTA with a custom block name. All three IFP formats are supported ANPK, ANP2, and ANP3. Unfortunately, GTA 3 animations are not supported, however, you can load GTA:VC IFP files using this function. You don't have to replace any animation to play a custom one, to play a custom animation, load the IFP file using this function, then use [SetPedAnimation|setPedAnimation](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/SetPedAnimation|setPedAnimation).

If you wish to replace a GTA internal animation with a custom one, you can use [EngineReplaceAnimation|engineReplaceAnimation](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/EngineReplaceAnimation|engineReplaceAnimation). To unload the IFP file, use [DestroyElement|destroyElement](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/DestroyElement|destroyElement), restarting or stopping the resource can also unload the IFP file automatically.}}

engineRequestModel.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0158|1.5.7|20147|This function is used to assign the next available model ID to a certain element type.}}

{{Tip|For most cases, you will probably want to add models to your server that are synced with all clients automatically. This is possible with this *resource*: [https://forum.multitheftauto.com/topic/133212-rel-add-new-models-library/ newmodels]}}

{{note|Vehicle unique features may be unsupported, see [https://github.com/multitheftauto/mtasa-blue/issues/1861 issue 1861] for examples and details}}

{{Important Note|Unlike some other functions, the side-effects of this function aren't reverted on resource stop, so you must manually call [engineFreeModel](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/engineFreeModel) in [onClientResourceStop](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientResourceStop) (Just like the example below does)}}

engineRestoreCOL.description:
&lt;!-- Change this to "Client function" or "Server function" appropriately--&gt;

&lt;!-- Describe in plain english what this function does. Don't go into details, just give an overview --&gt;

This function restores the original collision model of the given model ID. Reverses the effect of [engineReplaceCOL](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/engineReplaceCOL).

engineRestoreModel.description:
&lt;!-- Change this to "Client function" or "Server function" appropriately--&gt;

&lt;!-- Describe in plain english what this function does. Don't go into details, just give an overview --&gt;

This function restores the visual DFF model of the given model ID. This restores the result of [engineReplaceModel](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/engineReplaceModel).

engineStreamingFreeUpMemory.description:
{{Added feature/item|1.5.9|1.5.8|20901|This function frees up the streaming RAM memory.}}

* **Note:** This function isn't accurate. The function works more like ''try to free up at least this amount of bytes''. It usually ends up freeing everything that isn't currently needed (which, depending on the scenery might be 1-200 megabytes).

{{Important Note|*This function is meant for advanced users only, as it can lead to stability issues*. If you use it too often, the map might start to flicker.}}

engineStreamingSetMemorySize.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0160|1.6.0|21874|Sets the maximum amount of RAM [in bytes] that can be used for streaming}}

{{Tip|The `showmemstat` command can be used to see this value in real-time [You might have to scroll down using PgDown on your keyboard]}}

{{Tip|To restore to default value use [engineStreamingRestoreMemorySize](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/engineStreamingRestoreMemorySize)}}

{{Important Note|*This function is meant for advanced users only, as it can lead to stability issues*. Using a very high value might result in more crashes, while using a value too low might lead to frequent pop-in [and due to the way MTA works micro-stutter as well]}}

createLight.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0150|1.5.0|7048|This function creates a 3D [Element/Light|light](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Light|light) in the world.}}

{{Note|

* The direction of the light only has any effect if the light type is ''spot light''.

* One light will only apply illumination effects to [Element/Ped|peds](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Ped|peds), [Element/Player|players](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Player|players), wheels and number plates (like a emergency vehicle siren light does).

* Two or more lights will apply illumination effects to everything (excluding objects) that is in range of, at least, two of them.

}}

getLightColor.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0150|1.5.0|7048|

This function returns the color for a [Element/Light|light](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Light|light) element.

}}

getLightDirection.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0150|1.5.0|7048|

This function returns the direction for a [Element/Light|light](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Light|light) element.

}}

getLightRadius.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0150|1.5.0|7048|

This function returns the radius for a [Element/Light|light](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Light|light) element.

}}

getLightType.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0150|1.5.0|7048|

This function returns the type for a [Element/Light|light](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Light|light) element.

}}

setLightRadius.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0150|1.5.0|7048|

This function sets the radius for a [Element/Light|light](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Element/Light|light) element.

}}

getObjectMass.description:
{{Client_function}}

{{New feature/item|3.0132|1.3.2|5170|

This function returns the mass of a specified object.

}}

setObjectMass.description:
{{client_function}}

{{New feature/item|3.0132|1.3.2|5170|

This function sets the mass of a specified object. Changing the mass leads to a different movement behavior for especially dynamic objects.

}}

getPedCameraRotation.description:
{{client function}}

* **Note:** The camera rotation angle returned by this function is 360º - α (where α is the actual camera rotation angle). See example to know how to deal with this.

This function gets the current camera rotation of a [ped](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/ped).

givePedWeapon.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0141|1.4.1|6937|

This function gives the specified weapon to the specified ped. This function can't be used on players, use [giveWeapon](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/giveWeapon) for that.

This function is mainly useful for client side created peds however you can use it on a server side ped, though note that the weapon wouldn't be synced between clients unless your script gives the weapon to the ped on every client.

There is an optional argument to specify ammunition and whether to set as the current weapon. If you don't specify an ammo value it will give 30 ammo by default and for a melee weapon you can specify just 1 or above.

}}

{{Note|

*When setting ammo for [Weapon|weapons in slot](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Weapon|weapons in slot) 0,1,10,11 or 12 the maximum ammo is 1

*When setting ammo for [Weapon|weapons in slot](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Weapon|weapons in slot) 3,4,5 the ammo is added

*When setting ammo for [Weapon|weapons in slot](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/Weapon|weapons in slot) 2,6,7,8,9 and the slot weapon is changing, the ammo is replaced

}}

setPedCanBeKnockedOffBike.description:
This function controls if a ped can fall of his bike by accident - namely by banging into a wall.

{{Note | This effect is not synced for peds. When the ped falls off, he will not have exited the vehicle. To get it working you need to call it each time the ped is streamed in &amp; each time it gets a new syncer.}}

{{Note | The ped will not get knocked off a bike that is set damage proof through [setVehicleDamageProof](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/setVehicleDamageProof). Refer to the note on that method for more information.}}

setPedLookAt.description:
* **Note:** Avoid calling setPedLookAt every frame as this can cause bugs like being invincible to burning.

{{Important Note|For remote players, you have to use [https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/SetPedAimTarget setPedAimTarget] before setPedLookAt.}}

Makes a ped turn his head and look at a specific world position or element.

getLocalPlayer.description:
This function gets the player element of the client running the current script.

{{New feature/item|3.0110|1.1||

You should use predefined variable *localPlayer* instead of typing getLocalPlayer() for better readability.

}}

setPlayerHudComponentProperty.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0161|1.6.0|22868|This function allows for modifying HUD properties, such as text or bar color, position, size, and more.}}

* **Note:** Due to a rendering bug in GTA, setting transparency for text with outline or shadow causes a visual glitch, resulting in blurred/smudged text. Transparency only works correctly on text without outline and shadow.

{{Tip|If the characters are uneven after changing the font, you should set the *proportional* property to *true*}}

{{Tip|The health bar is positioned relative to its width, so after changing its width, its position on the X-axis will also change. If you want to maintain the bar's position, you also need to calculate its position based on its width. Additionally, the width is calculated depending on the MAX_HEALTH stat.}}

[File:HUD properties.png|thumb|right|Example of a modified HUD.](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/File:HUD properties.png|thumb|right|Example of a modified HUD.)

createProjectile.description:
This function creates a projectile of the specified type on the specified coordinates.

{{Note|

**Model* argument is not synchronized between clients. Clients differs from local player see always standard projectile model.

**Target* argument valid elements are: [player](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/player), [ped](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/ped), [vehicle](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/vehicle) and [object](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/object).

}}

svgCreate.description:
{{Added feature/item|1.5.9|1.5.8|20979|

Creates an [svg](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/svg) from size (blank document), filepath or raw data.

}}

{{Important Note|Before r21155 ([https://github.com/multitheftauto/mtasa-blue/commit/31579051cc046bc5cb55c59fc4e9e70ec1bdce34 3157905]) the provided callback was only fired *once* after the function had performed its task. This is no longer the case - each SVG can now store a single callback function (optional) which is fired *every time* the SVG texture has been changed/updated.}}

* **Note:** SVG in MTA is handled by the *lunasvg* rendering engine - Some features in MTA may not work properly, compared to the browser.

''Check the list of supported [https://github.com/sammycage/lunasvg?tab=readme-ov-file#features features].'''

{{Tip|If you are experiencing poor texture quality or artifacts in the form of black outlines, setting the blend mode to *add* might help}}

downloadFile.description:
{{New items|3.0140|1.4|

This function ensures the requested resource file is correct and then triggers [onClientFileDownloadComplete](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientFileDownloadComplete).  If the file has been previously downloaded and the CRC matches, the file will not be downloaded again but [onClientFileDownloadComplete](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientFileDownloadComplete) will still run. The *file* should also be included in the resource meta.xml with the *download* attribute set to "false", see [meta.xml](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/meta.xml) for more details.

}}

{{Tip|If you are only using [downloadFile](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/downloadFile) to download mod files after other resources, then do not use [downloadFile](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/downloadFile), and instead set&lt;br/&gt; '&lt;download_priority_group&gt;-1&lt;/download_priority_group&gt;' in the resource [meta.xml](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/meta.xml)}}

* **Note:** This function may cause performance issues with client and/or server.

{{Tip|Avoid using fileExists before calling [downloadFile](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/downloadFile). Always call [downloadFile](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/downloadFile) and handle the result in [onClientFileDownloadComplete](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/onClientFileDownloadComplete)}}

getLocalization.description:
{{New items|3.0140|1.4|

This function gets the player's localization setting as set in the MTA client.

}}

areVehicleLightsOn.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0158|1.5.7|19626|This function is used to find out whether the lights of the vehicle are on.}}

{{Note|

*This is different to [getVehicleOverrideLights](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/getVehicleOverrideLights) because this function will return *true* if the lights were turned on by natural causes.

* Unless [setVehicleOverrideLights](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/setVehicleOverrideLights) is used, vehicles always automatically disable their lights at 06:25 and enable them at 20:26.}}

getVehicleComponents.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0131|1.3.1|4748|

This function gets a table of the components currently on a [vehicle](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/vehicle).

}}

getVehicleComponentVisible.description:
{{New feature/item|4.0140|1.3.1|4715|

This function get component visibility for [vehicle](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/vehicle).

}}

getVehicleEntryPoints.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0161|1.6.0|22649|

This function returns a table containing the positions to 4 possible entry points to a vehicle. This function can be used alongside [setPedEnterVehicle](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/setPedEnterVehicle) to make a ped enter a specific seat by first moving the ped to a entry point retrieved through *getVehicleEntryPoints* and then using [setPedEnterVehicle](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/setPedEnterVehicle) to make them enter.

}}

* **Note:** This does not directly relate to the amount of doors a vehicle has as vehicles with two doors can have multiple entry points to the same door.

* **Note:** The vehicle needs to be streamed in for this function to work.

getVehicleModelDummyPosition.description:
