setVehicleWheelScale.description:
{{New feature/item|3.0158|1.5.7|20642|This function sets the scale of all the wheels of a [vehicle](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/vehicle). The wheel scale multiplies the visible height and length (but not width) of all the wheels in a vehicle, without affecting their collisions or the handling, similarly to [setVehicleComponentScale](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/setVehicleComponentScale). The wheel scale is applied after the [setVehicleModelWheelSize|model wheel size](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/setVehicleModelWheelSize|model wheel size).}}

* **Note:** Installing or removing a wheel upgrade from a vehicle resets the wheel scale to the default value.

{{Tip|The default value for vehicles without wheel upgrades is 1, which renders the wheels in the model as usual. On the other hand, the default value for vehicles with a wheel upgrade is the [setVehicleModelWheelSize|size of the wheels in the front axle](https://wiki.multitheftauto.com/wiki/setVehicleModelWheelSize|size of the wheels in the front axle) of the vehicle model.}}

